# Local Android release signing. See ../PLAY_STORE_READINESS_PLAN.md.
#
# Copy this file to `keystore.properties` in the same directory and fill it in.
# `keystore.properties` and every *.jks / *.keystore file are ignored by Git/EAS.
# Never commit the filled-in copy or the key itself.
#
# Use an existing upload key stored OUTSIDE the repository and backed up offline.
# EAS_BUILD=true skips local signing entirely; EAS manages its own credentials.
# The plugin never embeds these values in generated build.gradle. Gradle reads
# this file at configuration time: an absent file keeps the template signing
# config (normally debug, NOT Play-uploadable); incomplete config fails the build.
#
# Standard Java .properties syntax, decoded as UTF-8. Do not wrap values in quotes:
# quotes, apostrophes, $, and braces are literal data, NOT Groovy expressions.
# Escape each literal backslash as \\ (or use / in paths). Use \u0020 for a
# leading space. Keep values on one line. Never use real secrets in examples/tests.

# Absolute path to the .jks, or a path relative to the mobile/ directory.
storeFile=C:/path/to/existing-upload-key.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=waveform-upload
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
